  "summary": "Kondapalli toys are toys made of wood in Kondapalli of Krishna district,  Vijayawada in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh.",
  "description": "Kondapalli toys are toys made of wood in Kondapalli of Krishna district,  Vijayawada in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. Bommala Colony translates to Toys Colony in Kondapalli is the place where the art of crafting takes place. It was registered as one of the geographical indication handicraft from Andhra Pradesh as per Geographical Indications of Goods (Registration and Protection) Act, 1999.\n\nThis GI application was filed by LIGHT (LANCO Institute of General Humanitarian Trust) and Kondapalli Wooden Toys Manufacturers.These toys were one of the varieties of toys assembled in the houses during the festivals of Sankranti and Navratri and is referred as Bommala Koluvu.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Andhra Pradesh; registration 2007–08), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
